  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 254 AM EDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nConditions will remain wet and unsettled through the extended period \nas the previously discussed pattern remains in place through the \nweekend. During this time, the upper level trough over the eastern \nUS will deepen southward, with an associated front settling over the \nsoutheastern US. Easterly to southeasterly flow will continue across \nour region, with PWATs continuing to trend near normal or slightly \nabove normal (1.9-2.1 inch range). Each afternoon could bring \nscattered to numerous showers and storms, starting along the East \ncoast sea breeze boundary then proceeding inland into the late \nafternoon hours. Similarly to the short term period, gusty winds, \nheavy rainfall and frequent lightning will all remain possible \nhazards.\n\nStarting next week, once the trough and front progress eastward, \nmodels start to suggest the two flanking ridges over the US and \nwestern Atlantic will start to merge, extending across the entire \nregion. Afternoon showers and thunderstorms will remain likely each \nafternoon, with coverage maximized across the interior and southwest \nFL thanks to the continuing easterly flow. \n\nTemperatures through the period will remain seasonably hot, with \nhighs in the low to mid 90s each afternoon and overnight lows in the \nlow 80s across the coastlines, and mid 70s over the interior.",
